From 63ea36ef5d6c89e4dbaacc25a1e44eb278919540 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nightly <nightly@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 21:38:26 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] nightly: zgx from hoangvu12/zgx nightly-design-export, with
 the Design plugin's zgx PRs

#1392 builds the app (apps/zgx) and the engine against the combined zgx
pull request (#2110, 6d3a20fd, on zgx main). The nightly builds them
against hoangvu12/zgx's nightly-design-export branch at 6cc6cbfc instead:
the same zgx PRs cherry-picked onto zeron/zgx's own zgx pin, 06c6d56,
which the rest of the app is built and tested against:

- #2074 ui.load_font (and from base64), #2095 ui.decode_image,
  #2096 ui.write_file / ui.read_file of any bytes
- #2080 ui.render_canvas, its text in layers, with its fixes
- #2076, #2081, #2082: canvas text spacing and wrapping, c:image, c:shadow
- #2094 zgx-text: text shaping and measuring without the renderer
- #2097 / #2098: canvas text in drawing order, clipped and turned, with
  the fast path; radial and conic gradients; raster pan (#2100) and
  zoom (#2101); #2103 a canvas that pans and zooms draws its text into
  its raster, with the zoom thread's own text rasterizer
- #2110's Canvas::layers fix: text stays under an overlay drawn over
  bordered cards
- #2115 ui.zip, #2116 render_canvas JPEG/WebP, #2117 write_file append,
  #2118 render_canvas straight to a file
- #2119 a canvas's raster text keeps its glyphs and layouts (with the
  fonts-key fix); canvas culling and clip masks, zoom rasters a newer
  zoom supersedes, and a whole-board backdrop on zoom out; a canvas
  panned past its raster or zoomed drawn in 256-px tiles made off the frame,
  uploaded within about 4 ms a frame into reused textures

Every zgx line moves, apps/zgx's [patch] entries too, so the app and the
engine use one zgx. Both lockfiles re-resolve zgx's vendored crates at
the branch (zgx-harfrust, zgx-vte, zgx-alacritty-terminal as the pin
has them) and resolve --locked.
